  "duration": 88.62999725341797,
  "text": "So on the side of your Hawgeye camera, there's going to be three sections of lights. Those are power, strength, and carrier. So the Hawgeyes plug and play. There's no on or off switch. So as soon as you plug up your power cable, the power light will come on immediately. Once your antenna is connected, after just a few minutes, you will see your strength lights. And then after a few more minutes, once it has connectivity to the tower, your carrier light will come on, which means you can live stream the camera and you're ready to go. So we're talking about connectivity issues. And one of those things that we've previously discussed a little bit that can cause you connectivity issues is a faulty antenna cable. With improper transport, you can damage this little connection. And what I'm going to demonstrate is what may happen if you have a poor connection due to improper transport. So we're just going to pull this out just a little bit. So it's still connected and it's still plugged in, but it's come out just a little bit. I'm going to lay this back down just like it was, and what you're going to see is your strength lights drop down and you will even lose carrier, which means that you will have trouble with your live stream. It will lag on you, your service will drop out, or your camera may go inactive altogether. So these connections are something you always want to keep a close eye on and properly transport them so they won't cause you any problems in the future.",
